# PermiePortal — Cursor Rules

## Project
Astro 4 static site. No React. No SSR. TypeScript.
Voice: Dark satire, Heyoka archetype, anti-greenwashing. No corporate speak.
Tagline energy: "Burn the grasshole."

## Stack
- Frontend: Astro + Tailwind + vanilla JS
- Fonts: Bebas Neue (headers), Instrument Serif (body), Space Mono (labels/mono)
- Colors: --soil #0f0d0a, --lime #8fb83a, --rust #c4551a, --ash #b8b0a0, --paper #ede8dc
- Data: Static JSON in src/data/ (plants.json, pests.json, relationships.json)
- Seeds: YAML files in src/seeds/plants/ and src/seeds/pests/

## Data Workflow
Never edit src/data/*.json directly.
Always edit YAML in src/seeds/, then run: ./sync.sh
The converter (convert_permie_data.py) rebuilds all JSON and copies to src/data/.

## Plant YAML structure
See src/seeds/plants/moringa-data.yml as the canonical example.
Required fields: common_name, picture, scientific_name, family, zone,
ideal_temp_min, ideal_temp_max, min_temp, max_temp, perennial,
layers, plant_function, description, companions, avoid, pests

## Pest YAML structure  
See src/seeds/pests/pests-data.yml — all pests live in one file as a YAML array.
Required fields: name, slug, picture, scientific_name, description,
characteristics, control_methods (object with keys: organic_sprays,
biological_controls, cultural_practices, mechanical_physical, preventive_methods),
natural_enemies (array)

## Pest name matching
Pest references in plant YAML must match pest slugs exactly.
Run ./sync.sh --check to validate before committing.

## Image locations
Plant images: public/assets/plants/{filename}.jpg
Pest images: public/assets/pests/{filename}.jpg

## Do not
- Edit src/data/*.json directly
- Use React components
- Add client-side JS frameworks
- Change the color palette
- Use corporate or greenwash language
